 "google_page": "<html><script>AF_initDataCallback({key: 'ds:1', hash: '2', data:[[[\"120081008824328902\", \"Senior Software Engineer, Cloud AI/ML Infrastructure\", \"https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/signin?jobId=CiUAL2FckRDZ2pRvz46L9katNPsylT9qY6DHiqP41UHoHZHVKRXkEjsA9yzvgjxk-E9kCn0s0m5VuWKa6JnreeaeXc6FzgZDKQ8keRC3V-Ub4QdTB0ORj0_Zg_C-H6fkP2fj9g%3D%3D_V2&loc=TW&title=Senior+Software+Engineer\", [null, \"<ul>\\n<li>Optimize end-to-end performance on AI infrastructure across the full technical stack to ensure systems operate at peak capacity.</li>\\n<li>Conduct in-depth performance profiling, debugging, and troubleshooting of complex AI/ML training and inference workloads.</li>\\n<li>Build internal tools and software for AI/ML infrastructure to provide an exceptional developer experience.</li>\\n<li>Partner with cross-functional, cross-regional teams to ensure infrastructure delivers maximum value and drives customer success.</li>\\n<li>Deliver technical enablement and support for key cloud customers, dr\"], [null, \"<h3>Minimum qualifications:</h3><ul>\\n<li>Bachelor\\u2019s degree or equivalent practical experience.</li>\\n<li>5 years of experience with software development in one or more programming languages.</li>\\n<li>3 years of experience with end-to-end Machine Learning (e.g., model deployment, model evaluation, data processing, debugging).</li>\\n</ul><br><h3>Preferred qualifications:</h3><ul>\\n<li>Master's degree or PhD in Computer Science or a related technical field.</li>\\n<li>Experience with Generative AI, Large Language Models, or Machine Learning infrastructure, including model deployment, profiling, and pe\"], \"projects/gweb-careers-proto/tenants/60107626-8e00-0000-0000-0071646e0806/companies/ebbbf0d1-8121-483c-8f99-ee92597591fc\", null, \"Google\", \"en-US\", [[\"Taipei, Taiwan\", [\"No. 73, Section 5, Xinyi Rd, Ankang Village, Xinyi District, Taipei City, Taiwan 110\"], \"Ankang Village\", \"110\", \"Taipei City\", \"TW\"]], [null, \"<p>Google's software engineers develop the next-generation technologies that change how billions of users connect, explore, and interact with information and one another. Our products need to handle information at massive scale, and extend well beyond web search. We're looking for engineers who bring fresh ideas from all areas, including information retrieval, distributed computing, large-scale system design, networking and data storage, security, artificial intelligence, natural language processing, UI design and mobile; the list goes on and is growing every day. As a software engineer, you w\"], [2, 3, 4], [1794469020, 205000000], [1794611353, 533000000], [1794611353, 664000000], [null, \"In most instances, this position requires in-person interviews as part of the hiring process.<br><p>Google welcomes people with disabilities.</p>\"], null, null, [null, \"\"], [null, \"<ul>\\n<li>Bachelor\\u2019s degree or equivalent practical experience.</li>\\n<li>5 years of experience with software development in one or more programming languages.</li>\\n<li>3 years of experience with end-to-end Machine Learning (e.g., model deployment, model evaluation, data processing, debugging).</li>\\n</ul>\"], 2], [\"119623062231360198\", \"Site Readiness Technical Program Lead, Data Center Engineering\", \"https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/signin?jobId=CiUAL2FckZ__SAzs98SfOKjg4-GHNT7OWx3l-0Ihcll20pMT721XEjsA9yzvgmjQ5vPChlmAjtltk2fqG_2FXXgCb1gm66rwvZxaXD0HFlp7roElrZITJvSZyaVZDr91EG9h1Q%3D%3D_V2&loc=US&title=Site+Readiness+Technical+Program+Lead\", [null, \"<ul>\\n<li>Evaluate\\u00a0<span>potential\\u00a0</span>sites for power, cooling, structure, network and schedule risk. We own the data hall and mechanical/electrical data center scope.</li>\\n<li>Exhibit, rack-interface requirements and deviation approvals that turn Google's standards into contract terms.</li>\\n<li>Design liquid cooling and CDUs, power distribution and single lines, etc.</li>\\n<li>Track construction, commissioning and floor access gates across partner sites and engineering labs, and flagging risks before they hit the schedule.</li>\\n<li>Escalate and quality Tier 2/3 facility infrastructure escal\"], [null, \"<h3>Minimum qualifications:</h3><ul>\\n<li><div><div></div></div>Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Construction Management, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.</li>\\n<li>10 years of experience in technical program management, including 5 years leading data center, mission-critical facility, or industrial construction or commissioning programs.</li>\\n<li>10 years of experience leading multi-site programs with external partners, developers and contractors, with accountability for schedule and deliverables.</li>\\n<li>10 years of experience presenting to and influencing ex\"], \"projects/gweb-careers-proto/tenants/60107626-8e00-0000-0000-0071646e0806/companies/ebbbf0d1-8121-483c-8f99-ee92597591fc\", null, \"Google\", \"en-US\", [[\"Sunnyvale, CA, USA\", [\"Sunnyvale, CA, USA\"], \"Sunnyvale\", null, \"CA\", \"US\"]], [null, \"<p>A problem isn\\u2019t truly solved until it\\u2019s solved for all. That\\u2019s why Googlers build products that help create opportunities for everyone, whether down the street or across the globe. As a Technical Program Manager at Google, you\\u2019ll use your technical expertise to lead complex, multi-disciplinary projects from start to finish. You\\u2019ll work with stakeholders to plan requirements, identify risks, manage project schedules, and communicate clearly with cross-functional partners across the company. You're equally comfortable explaining your team's analyses and recommendations to executives as you ar\"], [2], [1794470884, 876000000], [1794611344, 133000000], [1794611344, 231000000], [null, \"\"], null, null, [null, \"\"], [null, \"<ul>\\n<li><div><div></div></div>Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Construction Management, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.</li>\\n<li>10 years of experience in technical program management, including 5 years leading data center, mission-critical facility, or industrial construction or commissioning programs.</li>\\n<li>10 years of experience leading multi-site programs with external partners, developers and contractors, with accountability for schedule and deliverables.</li>\\n<li>10 years of experience presenting to and influencing executives on schedule, risk and investment plans.</li>\\n</ul>\"], 3], [\"84688004404126406\", \"Software Engineering Manager, Remote Direct Memory Access Networking\", \"https://www.google.com/about/careers/applications/signin?jobId=CiUAL2FckS2xJyYsihXujnwOVGBI-P0p0rvW4n_c_0JM5wlpoN8IEjsA9yzvgk8u7BI7fw9JvGreEUSnsTzukgwYPlfkPyv1NnfKlsSRaN96H4r5CVvCDvQNY_OK-ijyzWXjog%3D%3D_V2&loc=US&title=Software+Engineering+Manager\", [null, \"<ul>\\n<li>Manage the Remote Direct Memory Access (RDMA) Networking DataPath team of 10+ engineers to deliver high-impact networking solutions.</li>\\n<li>Own the execution of cross-functional initiatives to deliver new offerings across Google Cloud and On-Premises AI/ML platforms.</li>\\n<li>Design, develop, and operate hardware-offloaded low-latency transport protocols including RDMA Over Converged Ethernet (RoCE) and Falcon.</li>\\n<li>Collaborate with team technical leads to establish short-term and long-term goals while driving roadmap innovations.</li>\\n<li>Align the team's work and deliverables \"], [null, \"<h3>Minimum qualifications:</h3><ul>\\n<li>Bachelor\\u2019s degree or equivalent practical experience.</li>\\n<li>8 years of experience in software development.</li>\\n<li>3 years of experience in a technical leadership role; overseeing projects.</li>\\n<li>Experience with computer architecture, debugging, performance analysis, and benchmarking.</li>\\n<li>Experience with HPC systems hardware architecture, network interconnect technologies and topologies, and HPC storage file systems.</li>\\n<li>Experience in low-level systems programming languages (e.g., C++ or C).</li>\\n</ul><br><h3>Preferred qualifications:</\"], \"projects/gweb-careers-proto/tenants/60107626-8e00-0000-0000-0071646e0806/companies/ebbbf0d1-8121-483c-8f99-ee92597591fc\", null, \"Google\", \"en-US\", [[\"Sunnyvale, CA, USA\", [\"Sunnyvale, CA, USA\"], \"Sunnyvale\", null, \"CA\", \"US\"]], [null, \"Like Google's own ambitions, the work of a Software Engineer goes beyond just Search. Software Engineering Managers have not only the technical expertise to take on and provide technical leadership to major projects, but also manage a team of Engineers. You not only optimize your own code but make sure Engineers are able to optimize theirs. As a Software Engineering Manager you manage your project goals, contribute to product strategy and help develop your team. Teams work all across the company, in areas such as information retrieval, artificial intelligence, natural language processing, dist\"], [3, 2, 4], [1794483476, 632000000], [1794611340, 514000000], [1794611340, 564000000], [null, \"In most instances, this position requires in-person interviews as part of the hiring process.\"], null, null, [null, \"\"], [null, \"<ul>\\n<li>Bachelor\\u2019s degree or equivalent practical experience.</li>\\n<li>8 years of experience in software development.</li>\\n<li>3 years of experience in a technical leadership role; overseeing projects.</li>\\n<li>Experience with computer architecture, debugging, performance analysis, and benchmarking.</li>\\n<li>Experience with HPC systems hardware architecture, network interconnect technologies and topologies, and HPC storage file systems.</li>\\n<li>Experience in low-level systems programming languages (e.g., C++ or C).</li>\\n</ul>\"], 3]], null, 3149, 20], sideChannel: {}});</script></html>",
